ved by summing the disjoint case counts in step total-count.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["complete-list"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"count-seven","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Exactly 7 subsets have sum 9.","step_ids":["total-count"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Verified in step example.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":["complete-list"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"example-subset","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"{1,8} is one requested subset with sum 9.","step_ids":["example"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived from the unique-largest-element partition and the complete case enumeration in step partition.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["complete-list"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"exhaustiveness","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The displayed list is exhaustive and contains no duplicates.","step_ids":["partition"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":["target-family"],"id":"largest-range","justification":"A member of F is nonempty and has a largest element m. If m is at most 3, its sum is at most 1+2+3=6, contradicting sum 9; since m belongs to the given ground set, m is at most 8.","statement":"For every member of F, its largest element m lies in {4,5,6,7,8}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["largest-range"],"id":"case-eight","justification":"The elements below 8 must sum to 1, and the only subset of {1,2,3,4,5,6,7} with sum 1 is {1}.","statement":"The m=8 case contributes exactly {1,8}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["largest-range"],"id":"case-seven","justification":"The elements below 7 must sum to 2, and the only subset of {1,2,3,4,5,6} with sum 2 is {2}.","statement":"The m=7 case contributes exactly {2,7}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["largest-range"],"id":"case-six","justification":"The elements below 6 must sum to 3. The only subsets o